# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The /vs/* section was removed 2026-08-22. Each page carried only 108-355 words
# of unique data on a shared template, and seven of them competed directly with a
# far stronger /alternatives page for the same competitor intent (for example
# /vs/outrank at 501 rendered words against /alternatives/outrank at 2,989).
# Redirecting rather than deleting keeps whatever link equity those indexed URLs
# hold and avoids ten crawl errors.
#
# Seven cannibalisation pairs, each to its stronger counterpart:
/vs/outrank            /alternatives/outrank         301
/vs/search-atlas       /alternatives/search-atlas    301
/vs/contentbird        /alternatives/contentbird     301
/vs/rankyak            /alternatives/rankyak         301
/vs/shopify-magic      /alternatives/shopify-magic   301
/vs/describely         /alternatives/describely      301
/vs/seowind            /alternatives/seowind         301

# Three had no /alternatives counterpart, so they go to the hub rather than 404.
/vs/surfer-seo         /alternatives                 301
/vs/jasper             /alternatives                 301
/vs/semrush            /alternatives                 301

# Hub and any straggler under /vs.
/vs                    /alternatives                 301
/vs/*                  /alternatives                 301

# Removed 2026-08-22. Both were templated industry pages carrying only ~110-130
# words of unique copy: /for/saas is off-ICP (the ICP is agencies broadly with
# e-commerce as the lead vertical) and /for/agencies restated the homepage pitch.
# /for/ecommerce survives, so /for/saas goes to the home page rather than to it,
# which would send a SaaS visitor to a store-specific page.
/for/saas              /                             301
# Repointed 2026-09-02. /agency-blueprint is now the agency page in substance:
# it carries the workspace, white-label, roles and approval detail plus the
# first-party scan, so an agency visitor belongs there rather than on the home
# page. Deliberately NOT renaming /agency-blueprint itself: the URL has been
# sent to prospects as an outreach artifact, it is paired with /it/agency-blueprint
# via hreflang, and a slug is a far weaker signal than the title and body it
# would cost two more redirects to change.
/for/agencies          /agency-blueprint             301

# /integrations/* removed 2026-08-22: three templated pages of 120-141 unique
# words each. The home page carries the integrations feature block, so it is the
# closest surviving equivalent.
/integrations          /                             301
/integrations/*        /                             301
